5. NO LEGAL ADVICE — PROFESSIONAL RESPONSIBILITY REMAINS WITH THE LICENSEE

THIS IS THE MOST IMPORTANT TERM IN THIS AGREEMENT.

The Suite is a drafting and workflow tool. It is not a lawyer, does not practice
law, and does not provide legal advice. Legal Authority Lab is not engaged in the
practice of law and forms no attorney-client relationship with the Licensee or
with any client of the Licensee.

The Licensee is solely responsible for:

  (a) the legal sufficiency, accuracy, and completeness of every document produced
      with the assistance of the Suite;
  (b) independently verifying every statute, rule, court decision, deadline, and
      procedural requirement before relying on it — the Suite marks authorities
      with a verification warning precisely because verification is the
      Licensee's duty and cannot be delegated to software;
  (c) confirming local judicial, division, circuit, county, and clerk practice,
      which changes without notice;
  (d) compliance with the Rules Regulating The Florida Bar, including the duties
      of competence, confidentiality, candor, supervision of nonlawyer assistance,
      and any applicable disclosure obligations concerning the use of artificial
      intelligence;
  (e) all attorney review and approval gates identified in the Suite.

The Suite deliberately does not cover certain subject areas, including trust
accounting, conflicts-of-interest screening, withdrawal and termination ethics,
limited-scope representation ethics, and attorney advertising compliance. Those
areas remain entirely the Licensee's responsibility. See
skills/lal-florida-ethics/references/coverage-and-limits.md.

No output of the Suite may be filed, served, or sent to a client, a court, or an
opposing party without review by a licensed Florida attorney.


